{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 american biographical drama film directed by david fincher and written by alexander payne, jesse armstrong, and charlie macleod. the film is based on the book \"the accidental billionaire\" by ben mezrich, which tells the story of the founding of the social networking site facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed.\n\nthe film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and former CEO of facebook. the film also stars andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, justin timberlake as sean parker, and josh hutcherson as andrew mccollum.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, creating a website called \"facemash\" which becomes a huge success. however, the site is eventually shut down by the university due to its popularity. this incident sparks the idea of creating a new site that will allow students to create their own profiles and connect with each other.\n\nmark meets eduardo and andrew, and they come up with the idea of creating a new site called \"facebook.\" however, their relationship with sean parker, a former harvard student who had previously created a similar site called \"friendster,\" becomes complicated. sean is approached by mark and his friends to help them with the new site, but sean's intentions are not entirely pure.\n\nthe film explores the themes of friendship, betrayal, and the consequences of success. it also delves into the complexities of mark's character, who is portrayed as a complex and sometimes difficult person to be around.\n\none of the strengths of the film is its performances. jesse eisenberg delivers a standout performance as mark zuckerberg, capturing his awkwardness and intensity. andrew garfield is also excellent as eduardo, bringing a sense of vulnerability and sensitivity to the character.\n\nthe film's direction by david fincher is also noteworthy. he brings a sense of cool and detached style to the film, which suits the subject matter perfectly. the cinematography by jeff cronkite is also impressive, capturing the beauty and complexity of the harvard university campus.\n\nthe film's score by trent reznor and atticus ross is also noteworthy. it is a haunting and atmospheric soundtrack that perfectly complements the film's themes and tone.\n\none of the criticisms of the film is that it takes some creative liberties with the true story. however, this is not necessarily a bad thing, as it allows the film to explore the themes and ideas in a more dramatic and engaging way.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-made and engaging film that explores the complexities of the facebook phenomenon. it is a must-see for anyone interested in the history of social media and the people who created it.\n\nrating: 4.5 out of 5 stars\n\nduration: 120 minutes\n\nrelease date: october 1, 2010\n\ngenre: biographical drama\n\nlanguage: english\n\ncountry: united states", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.045232724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0016868184}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -7.6293654e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.18040486}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.00012385078}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.32515162}, {"token": "201", "logprob": -2.9086643e-05}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -3.933899e-06}, {"token": " american", "logprob": -0.3342006}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -0.0031711787}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -0.00043990472}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.011117537}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.00057299406}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.18416922}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0021900972}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -0.009290322}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -0.00041380903}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": -2.682173e-05}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2561861}, {"token": " written", "logprob": -0.0026351034}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -3.3378547e-